<p>A puzzle from Peter Winkler&#8217;s excellent <em>Mathematical Puzzles</em> (2021):</p>
<p>A certain island contains a network of roads. Each road segment (between one intersection and the next) has its own name. If <em>d</em> is the average number of road segments that meet at an intersection, show that it&#8217;s possible to take a drive on the island that traverses at least <em>d</em> road segments and hits them in alphabetical order.</p>

